    "CVE-2026-78002"
  ],
  "summary": "## Summary",
  "details": "## Summary\r\n\r\nrsyslog contains a heap buffer overflow in the RainerScript `replace()` function; the three-argument form of `wrap()` uses the same implementation.\r\n\r\nWhen a replacement expression encounters certain partial matches, the implementation can calculate an output buffer size that is smaller than the data subsequently written to it. The issue occurs when a ruleset applies `replace()` or three-argument `wrap()` to attacker-controlled message content.\r\n\r\n## Impact\r\n\r\nAn unauthenticated remote sender can trigger heap corruption and cause `rsyslogd` to terminate when network input is processed by an affected ruleset. The reported and independently reproduced impact is denial of service. Confidentiality loss, integrity loss, and code execution have not been demonstrated.\r\n\r\n## Affected configurations and versions\r\n\r\nVersions 8.6.0 through 8.2608.0 are affected.\r\n\r\nThe vulnerable code is part of rsyslog core, but exposure requires a configuration that applies `replace()` or three-argument `wrap()` to untrusted message data received from a network input.\r\n\r\n## Remediation\r\n\r\nUpdate to the **2026-08-24 daily stable build** or a later release containing the fix.\r\n\r\nAs a temporary mitigation, do not apply `replace()` or three-argument `wrap()` to untrusted message content.\r\n\r\n## Credit\r\n\r\nReported by DavidKorczynski. The issue was found by Anthropic using Claude and manually validated by Ada Logics.\r\n\r\n## References\r\n\r\n- CVE-2026-78002",
